@Gateway_HostAddress = http://localhost:5000
@Catalog_HostAddress = http://localhost:5001
@Order_HostAddress = http://localhost:5002
@Seq_HostAddress = http://localhost:5341

# ==============================================================================
# ShopMicro End-to-End Distributed Trace Pipeline Verification (Task 7.4)
#
# This file exercises the complete distributed request lifecycle:
# 1. Gateway (Port 5000): Ingests the initial HTTP request.
# 2. Order API (Port 5002): Routed by Gateway, creates order.
# 3. Catalog API (Port 5001): Called by Order API via resilient HttpClient.
# 4. RabbitMQ (Port 5672): Receives published OrderCreatedEvent.
# 5. Notification Worker: Consumes event asynchronously & performs idempotent dispatch.
# 6. Seq (Port 5341): Centralizes all structured logs & OpenTelemetry distributed trace spans.
# ==============================================================================

### 1. Gateway Route Verification - Query Catalog Products via Gateway
# Gateway routes '/catalog/{**catch-all}' directly to Catalog.Api (port 5001).
GET {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/catalog/products
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Create Product in Catalog via Gateway
# Creates a test product that will be ordered in Step 3.
# Notice the custom W3C traceparent header to establish the root trace.
# @name createProduct
POST {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/catalog/products
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
traceparent: 00-4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736-00f067aa0ba902b7-01

{
  "name": "Ultra-Wide Gaming Monitor",
  "description": "34-inch curved OLED monitor",
  "price": 799.99,
  "categoryName": "Displays"
}

###

### 3. Place Order via Gateway (Full End-to-End Distributed Trace)
# Trace Flow:
# [Gateway:5000] -> [Order.Api:5002] -> [Catalog.Api:5001] -> [RabbitMQ:5672] -> [Notification.Worker]
#
# Replace {{productId}} with the product ID returned in Step 2.
@productId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
traceparent: 00-4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736-00f067aa0ba902b7-01

{
  "customerEmail": "alex.dev@example.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}

###

### 4. Fetch Placed Order via Gateway
# Retrieves the order persisted in SQL Server through the Gateway route.
@orderId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 5. Inspect Traces & Logs in Seq
# Query Seq for the unified Trace ID across all 4 services.
GET {{Seq_HostAddress}}/api/events?filter=@TraceId%20%3D%20'4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736'
Accept: application/json

###
